    "title": "Why the completed metformin charges were different",
    "body": "The completed charges are established by two paid pharmacy claims for metformin 500 mg tablets, 60 tablets for a 30-day supply. On August 18, 2026, Oak Street Pharmacy processed the claim with the preferred retail cost-share category, and the member paid $8.00. On September 16, 2026, Lakeview Pharmacy processed the claim with the standard retail cost-share category, and the member paid $27.00.\n\nThe pharmacy classifications match the applied cost-share categories: Oak Street Pharmacy was classified as preferred retail, and Lakeview Pharmacy was classified as standard retail. The selected policy for this plan and period states that the matched 30-day metformin 500 mg supply is $8 at preferred retail and $27 at standard retail under the recorded conditions.",
